  "headline": "Estimated-parameter (Phase-II) run-length degradation of the EWMA(0.20,3) and two-sided CUSUM(0.5,5) arms of the live three-detector union, via the exact conditional reduction Y ~ N(-U/W, 1/W^2) (Jones-Champ-Rigdon 2001/2004) with Brook-Evans Markov-chain ARL solvers generalized to non-unit variance. The memory detectors degrade MORE than Shewhart: at a 30-observation baseline the guaranteed (5th-pct) ARL0 retains only 9.5% (EWMA) and 9.8% (CUSUM) of its known-parameter value versus 13.3% for Shewhart, and the guaranteed (95th-pct) union false-alarm count over the module's 30-batch KPI window rises from the known-parameter 0.199 to 1.73991 -- outside the locked budget of 1.5.",
